<vertex eid="9"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered Yes" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">P03 [YES]
Twelve-cell finite execution exists?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">P03 | Twelve-cell finite execution exists?

Status: YES

Method: Functional isolation / staged execution

Scope / coordinates: SP8 12-cell subset: four incident cells plus eight selected isolated cells; use successful retained attempts, not killed attempts.

Remaining search space: At least one actual finite execution exists for this subset, or only construction/projections exist.

Binary predicate: The saved 12-cell evidence contains a completed real finite runtime after initialization.

Decision limit: Completed real run and finite traces, with measured duration/load/attempt retained.

Recorded observation: Attempt 3 completed 1 ms at dt 0.005 ms in both ei and disconnected configurations with finite traces; conductance probes were zero in both. Earlier killed attempts remain untested.

YES: Retain the measured subset as the runtime boundary.

NO: Keep execution open despite construction success.

Next check: Report the selected attempt's measured configuration; do not extrapolate qualification to 40 or 104 cells.

Unresolved after either answer: Includes isolated cells and borrowed profiles; runtime is not physiological coverage.

